#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# rows

#% text
# `rows(ds)` gives the list of the rows of the dataset `ds`, each an association from column names to values.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `dataset(rows(ds))` is `ds` again.

#% item
# A row is the value functions such as `select`, `sort_by` and `add_column` pass to their function argument.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
rows(dataset(assoc("x" -> [1, 2], "y" -> ["a", "b"])))
#% output
#= [assoc("x" -> 1, "y" -> "a"), assoc("x" -> 2, "y" -> "b")]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Part notation gives one row:

#% cell
ds = dataset(assoc("x" -> [1, 2], "y" -> ["a", "b"]))
ds[2] === rows(ds)[2]
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `dataset`, `column`, `columns`
